{
 "summary": "Checkout p95 latency rose above 1s at 00:27:22Z on gateway, orders and inventory at the same moment, peaking near 2.4s, with no 5xx errors. Sampled slow checkout traces put most self time in inventory POST /reserve (release 3.1.5), so the latency starts in inventory and the upstream services are only waiting on it. Logs and deployment records came back empty, so why inventory slowed is not yet known.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory's POST /reserve operation (release 3.1.5) slowed down, and checkout requests waited on it through orders and gateway. The trigger for that slowdown is not identified in the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-52f825c98c5f",
   "ev-506ce368ec1d"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway and orders p95 latency crossed 1s at the same timestamp as inventory, 00:27:22Z, and peaked at similar values (about 2.4s). This fits callers waiting on a downstream dependency.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7ee29eff609f",
    "ev-d850cf508436",
    "ev-506ce368ec1d"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Request rates on gateway, orders and inventory were higher at the end of the window than the window average (for example, gateway 2.08 rps last vs 1.84 avg). Load may have contributed to inventory slowness, but the evidence does not show a causal link.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-7ee29eff609f",
    "ev-506ce368ec1d",
    "ev-d850cf508436"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
